        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-09-13T07:58:32+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-growth-product-manager-london-168924/1>,
        <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fyxer/growth-product-manager-london-168924> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "3f1a987049f35a2f6b902a5a1004b90f733f45cedf705f16e6cd990d9795350a" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-09-13T07:58:32+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-09-13T07:58:32+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:reconciliationReason "no reviewed first-party candidate" ;
    kgjobs:sourceOccurrence <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-growth-product-manager-london-168924/1> ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "growth-product-manager-london-168924" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-13"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About Fyxer Since launching in May 2024 we've grown to $30 million in ARR. Fyxer is building an AI executive assistant that handles emails, scheduling and follow-up, freeing people in client-facing roles to focus on their customers. The Mission At Fyxer, we believe the only sustainable competitive advantage for a startup is the quality and speed of execution. We are looking for a full-stack product thinker who uses research, data, and experimentation to drive better bets, faster learning, and stronger commercial outcomes. We’re not looking for someone to write specs and hand over insights. We want someone who helps us think better and decide better. You’ll drive product vision and strategy of a product domain alongside our product, growth and leadership teams. The Role You’ll drive product vision and strategy of a product domain / category design alongside our product / growth and leadership teams. You will operate at speed. We care about generating signals quickly, making informed decisions, and learning fast. You are comfortable working with imperfect information and tightening thinking as you go. You will have significant autonomy. We expect strong judgment, clear communication, and ownership of outcomes and a fullstack background around A/B experimentation and everything that comes with it. What you will own: You will own the quality of our product bets and the speed at which we learn. Turn ambiguity into direction. Take messy signals from customers, product data, and the market and translate them into clear problem framing and product strategy. Work directly with engineers. You will partner closely with engineers and founders from the start of an initiative, shaping solutions together rather than handing over specs. Use the right tools to validate ideas and reduce risk: interviews, prototypes, experiments, product analytics, fake doors, usability testing, and behavioural analysis Ship, learn, and iterate quickly. Move product bets from idea to shipped product to measurable outcomes, continuously tightening the loop between learning and building. Raise the bar of product thinking across the team by coaching others, introducing scalable frameworks, and helping the team stay close to customers Who You Are Expert: You are an expert in your domain specialization that everyone could learn from including our other PM’s Systems thinker: You understand customer journeys, funnels, and feedback loops. You connect user behaviour to outcomes and revenue impact, not just isolated features. Engineering partner: You work closely with engineers and founders, translating user insight into clear problem framing and practical tradeoffs. You influence what we build through evidence and clarity. Decision oriented: You know when there is enough signal to move. You help others clarify thinking, sharpen hypotheses, and make confident calls under uncertainty. Capability builder: You design product systems that compound over time rather than one off projects. Your work levels up how we do product and discovery across the company, and you introduce frameworks, coach others, and build repeatable learning loops. Why Fyxer? We are intentional about our team. We believe a small, exceptional team working with extreme focus will always outperform a large, bloated organization. Autonomy: We hire people who want ownership and then we actually give it to them. Scope: This is a rare opportunity to join a high-growth rocket ship at the foundational stage.. Velocity: You will be fast-tracked into senior responsibilities far earlier than at a traditional company. Compensation: £140K – £180K • £140K – £180K Equity • £140K – £180K • £140K – £180K Equity Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
