    schema:description "<p><strong>Digital Content Consultant<br></strong>London, hybrid<br>6 month FTC&nbsp;</p> <p><em>DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.</em></p> <p><strong>JOB PURPOSE</strong>&nbsp;</p> <p>Working with customers pursuing personalisation at scale, an optimal content supply chain is a necessity.&nbsp; With the emergence of generative AI and its potential to supercharge the supply of hyper personalised&nbsp; content we are seeking a Senior Content Supply Consultant to help customers assess, optimise and manage their content supply processes, delivering content seamlessly and&nbsp; efficiently to execute outstanding consumer experiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>WHAT YOU’LL DO&nbsp;</strong></p> <ul> <li>Lead inspiring business discovery workstreams and align with customers on relevant business&nbsp; goals and critical metrics&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Map the content lifecycle from creation to distribution, including all stages and touchpoints.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Assess the customer’s content supply process to identify inefficiencies and bottlenecks&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Define the role of Generative AI and automation capabilities to reduce cost and time to create,&nbsp; produce and deliver content&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Perform complex process re-design to align the content supply process to a customer’s strategy&nbsp; and drive dramatic improvements in productivity, cycle time, quality, and customer satisfaction.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Define workflows to outline the sequence of tasks, responsibilities, dependencies, and approvals&nbsp; required to move content from one stage to the next.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Guide customers to train AI models on data to ensure a consistent and aligned brand representation across channels&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Help customers to assess current brand guidelines and define AI integration objectives, develop&nbsp; AI-specific guidelines, train the team and implement monitoring and evaluation processes.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Design effective content approval processes to ensure published content aligns with a customer’s&nbsp; policies and expectations.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Develop the implementation strategy &amp; roadmap in partnership with Technical Architects and customer teams for Adobe solutions that enable content supply, e.g. Adobe Experience Manager,&nbsp; Workfront, Creative Cloud, Express, Frame.io etc&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Research and define relevant content performance and content process benchmarks&nbsp;</li> <li>Design and implement content performance and content process reporting mechanisms to&nbsp; monitor progress against KPIs&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Analyse performance and surface insights informing continued optimisation and validating&nbsp; business outcomes.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Perform organisational analysis to assess barriers to adoption and develop mitigation strategies.&nbsp; Advise and lead customers through the change required to adopt optimised content tools and&nbsp; processes across the customer org and involved 3rd parties&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Identify and enable customers teams on the required capability, functionality and features across&nbsp; Adobe technologies that facilitate content supply requirements with a specialist focus on Adobe&nbsp; Experience Manager and Workfront&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Support the enablement of customer teams across roles, responsibilities and process that&nbsp; facilitate the customer’s optimised content supply chain.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Continually grow your footprint and role within the client engagement and relationship.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><strong>WHAT YOU’LL BRING&nbsp;</strong></p> <ul> <li>5+ Years of content supply optimisation experience – as a Product Owner, Product Manager or&nbsp; Lead Business Consultant&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>The ability to translate business requirements into a technical solution and an understanding of&nbsp; how to leverage content solutions to meet business needs is important.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>A deep understanding of Content Management platforms and technologies (AEM, Workfront&nbsp; preferred) from a business perspective and standard methodologies around implementations.&nbsp; AEM + Workfront Certified Business Practitioner.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Complex process re-design expertise coupled with change management experience.&nbsp; ξ Experience with AI and automation with a strong understanding of how AI, machine learning, and&nbsp; generative AI can revolutionise the content supply chain.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Experience with AI model training and the development of processes to secure adherence to&nbsp; brand standards&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Understanding or experience in using productised APIs, SaaS, SOA, Cloud Services, and Content&nbsp; Management Systems is beneficial&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Extensive Agile experience and with product backlog management experience&nbsp; Customer-centric approach&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Outcome mentality and strong ability to plan for and realise business value.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Demonstrated experience working with business users and senior stakeholders, software&nbsp; engineers, application architects and digital marketing agencies&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Clear written and verbal communication skills presenting outcomes, sharing information, and&nbsp; leading meetings&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><strong>WE OFFER:</strong></p> <ul> <li>A flexible, hybrid working policy (2 days from the office, depending on location).</li> <li>An excellent salary based on experience and equal pay policies</li> <li>Pension, free private healthcare, mental health support, and company sick pay scheme.</li> <li>26 days paid holiday (plus UK Bank Holidays).</li> <li>Help getting you to work with a season ticket loan and cycle to work scheme.</li> <li>Enhanced family friendly policies to support new parents.</li> <li>Social and Cultural Events, plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues through organised activities and celebrations.</li> <li>Inspirational Talks, bringing the outside in with regular guest speakers and events.</li> <li>Learning and Development, supporting your growth with continuous opportunities to learn and advance.</li> <li>Buddy Programme: You will be paired with a ‘Buddy’ to help you through your first weeks’ at DEPT®.</li> <li>A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified <a href=\"https://www.deptagency.com/en-gb/insight/dept-is-a-certified-b-corporation/\">B Corp® since 2021</a> and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.</li> <li>Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!</li> <li>The opportunity for possibility. We want to enable you to do what you do best and help you develop your skills further with training, development and certifications.</li> <li>Global annual <a href=\"https://www.deptagency.com/dept-cares-day-2023/\">DEPT® Cares Month</a> in which employees come together and donate their skills to support local charities.</li> </ul> <p><strong>WHY DEPT®?</strong></p> <p>We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.</p> <p>We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.</p> <p>At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build.</p> <p><strong>DIVERSITY, EQUITY &amp; INCLUSION&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.</p> <p>Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.</p> <p>We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.</p> <p>Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts <a href=\"https://www.deptagency.com/the-good-company/\">here</a>.</p> Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
