    schema:description "Overview We are looking for a motivated Working Student IT Administration to join our IT Administration team. This is a great opportunity to gain practical, hands-on experience in corporate IT alongside your studies, in a hybrid role that offers flexibility and real responsibility from day one. Your Role Supports the IT Administration team in ensuring the smooth day-to-day operation of internal IT systems, hardware and workplace technology Assists with employee IT support by helping with hardware setup, software installation, user account management and basic troubleshooting Supports onboarding and offboarding activities by preparing devices, managing access requests and maintaining IT equipment Helps maintain IT inventory, hardware documentation, software licenses and internal records Assists with basic system administration tasks, device management, and office IT infrastructure under the guidance of the IT Administration Team Lead Contributes to improving IT documentation, knowledge base articles and internal processes Works closely with colleagues across the company to provide friendly and reliable IT support while gaining practical experience in corporate IT administration Your Profile Currently enrolled in a Bachelor's or Master's program in Computer Science, Information technology, Business Informatics or a related field Basic understanding of computer hardware, operating systems, networks and common workplace software Interest in IT support, systems administration and learning about enterprise IT environments Hands-on, reliable and eager to solve technical problems and support colleagues Structured way of working with good organizational skills and attention to detail Strong communication skills and a service-oriented mindset Fluent in English; German is a plus Nice To Have Active Directory M365 (Exchange Online, Sharepoint, Teams) Microsoft Intune Github Terraform Why you will love working with us Work-life balance: Enjoy our flexible processes that allow you to work in a hybrid mode: either from home, your workation or our Berlin office, as we love to meet and connect from time to time in person. On top of that, we also offer 30 paid vacation days Based in the heart of Berlin: Our spacious and loft-style headquarters is located in a historic building at the heart of Berlin, with a nice view of the TV Tower and convenient connections to all parts of the city – thanks to U1, U2, U6, M41 and S-Bahn at Anhalter Bahnhof Learning & development: A team that fosters growth and values knowledge sharing. With dedicated training days, learning subscriptions, a personal development budget and clear growth goals, we’ll empower you to reach your next career milestone and beyond! Team events: Coffee Breaks, Chats ‘n’ Cheers, Brunches, All-Hands Meetings: our company culture is vivid and open for new ideas that are inclusive, diverse and fun! Competitive compensation: Excellent people deserve great working conditions. We conduct annual compensation reviews to ensure that we are paying salaries above the market average Perks: Urban Sports Club discount, company pension subsidy, discounts, subsidized public transport ticket: our teams enjoy numerous perks beyond the fruit basket and coffee flat rate Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow" ;
